## Methodology

W44-185 zenjxl bench surfaced `3637739` as the dominant Zenjxl
Pareto-loser: 83 strict-loss cells (bytes>+1% AND ssim2<-0.1) across
100 cells/image (5 efforts × 20 distances). Other photos follow the
same pattern at lower frequencies:

  3637739: 83 strict-loss cells (LOSER_DOMINANT)
  7062219: 51 (LOSER_DOMINANT)
  1420710: 43 (LOSER_HEAVY)
  297394:  37 (LOSER_HEAVY)
  1475938: 35 (LOSER_HEAVY)
  1531677: 30 (LOSER_HEAVY)
  1189261: 25 (LOSER_MILD)
  1025469: 22 (LOSER_MILD)
  1418519: 11 (WINNER — bytes-negative on most cells)
  2389166:  7 (WINNER)

W44-198 ran two read-only probes to test whether a zenanalyze-driven
discriminator + W44-29 entropy_mul lift could close the cluster.

## Step 1: Feature space probe (w44_198_loser_probe)

Computed 28 candidate features for all 41 CID22 validation photos.
Below: the relevant 9 images (LOSER + WINNER classes) with key features:

  class             image       m3_colour  fcbr    edge_dens mask_med  mean_luma
  LOSER_DOMINANT   3637739     12.21      0.092   0.296     75.83    147.15
  LOSER_DOMINANT   7062219     51.14      0.011   0.633     47.79    103.60
  LOSER_HEAVY      1420710     32.93      0.000   0.930     39.55    155.53
  LOSER_HEAVY      297394     103.70      0.096   0.480     62.00    137.04
  LOSER_HEAVY      1475938     21.70      0.360   0.220     89.32    186.46
  LOSER_HEAVY      1531677     12.29      0.000   0.877     35.63     78.56
  LOSER_MILD       1189261     98.84      0.003   0.490     69.08    121.83
  LOSER_MILD       1025469     45.45      0.017   0.172     76.08     84.24
  WINNER           1418519     36.84      0.098   0.164     92.33    194.88
  WINNER           2389166     47.99      0.134   0.441     46.24     71.37

Critical observation: 3637739 has features OPPOSITE 1418519 on
edge_density (0.296 vs 0.164) and identical-class on mask_med (75 vs
92, both "high mask"). NO single feature axis cleanly separates
LOSER_DOMINANT from WINNER. The 8 LOSER images span the entire feature
range: m3 ∈ [12, 104], fcbr ∈ [0.000, 0.360], edge_density ∈ [0.17,
0.93], mask_med ∈ [36, 89], mean_luma ∈ [78, 186].

## Step 2: Existing gate cross-reference

Checked which W44 gates currently fire on each LOSER:

  Image     mask_med  Existing W44 gates firing                      n_loss
  3637739   75.83     NONE (mask>50, m3<80, edge_density<0.7)         83
  7062219   47.79     W44-29 (mask<50)                                51
  1420710   39.55     W44-29 (mask<50), W44-96 variant Z (m3>=25)     43
  297394    62.00     NONE                                            37
  1475938   89.32     NONE                                            35
  1531677   35.63     W44-29, W44-96 variant Z (LC m3<25)             30
  1189261   69.08     W44-91 (mask∈[50,80] + m3>=80 + fcbr<0.01)      25
  1025469   76.08     NONE                                            22
  1418519   92.33     W44-166 variant Z (mask_p25=88>=85)             11
  2389166   46.24     W44-29                                          7

Pattern: 4 LOSER images have NO gate firing (3637739, 297394, 1475938,
1025469). 5 LOSER images already fire at least one gate. The 2 WINNER
images are admitted to specialized variant Z gates (1418519) or W44-29
(2389166).

## Step 3: Forced-lift A/B (w44_198_forced_lift_probe)

If the W44-29 mechanism is the right lever for the LOSER cluster,
forcing the lift ON via `high_d_photo_hint = Some(true)` on
LOSER images where the gate doesn't fire (3637739, 297394, 1475938)
should close the deficit. Measured on 5 images × 4 distances × 2 efforts.

Results (Δb_vs_AUTO and ΔSSIM2_vs_AUTO when forcing W44-29 lift ON):

  Image    mask_class       e5d2    e5d3    e5d4    e5d5    e7d2    e7d3    e7d4    e7d5
  3637739  mask76_NOGATE    +0.85  -0.11  -0.02  -0.69  -0.16  -1.67  -1.54  +1.01  ← Δb%
                            -0.01  -0.32  -0.07  +0.02  +0.06  -0.25  +0.03  -0.07  ← ΔSSIM2
  7062219  mask48_FIRES     +0.45  +0.00  +0.00  +0.00  -1.23  +0.00  +0.00  +0.00  ← Δb% (FORCE = AUTO)
  1420710  mask40_FIRES     -1.24  +0.00  +0.00  -0.62  -3.16  +0.00  +0.00  +0.11
  297394   mask62_NOGATE    +0.27  -0.06  +1.21  -2.34  -0.15  +1.14  -0.91  +1.59
                            -0.05  -0.07  -0.28  +0.02  -0.05  -0.10  -0.31  +0.92
  1475938  mask89_NOGATE    -0.89  -0.70  -0.34  -3.42  +1.38  -0.91   N/A    N/A

Best 3637739 cell: e7 d=3 saves -1.67% bytes but COSTS -0.25 SSIM2 →
still strict-loser. Best e7 d=4 saves -1.54% bytes ΔSSIM2 neutral but
the gap is +6.24% — fix closes 1/4 of gap at best.

For 7062219 (gate already fires), FORCE has zero effect because AUTO
already takes the gated path — the lift is deployed but the gap
remains +2-6%.

**Conclusion: The W44-29 entropy_mul lift mechanism is NOT the lever
for the 3637739-class strict-loser cluster.** Even when forced on,
gains are marginal (<1.7% bytes, no SSIM2 improvement) and cannot
close the +5-7% byte gap.

## Honest-stop decision

W44-198 HONEST-STOPS on the discriminator-based fix approach. The
root cause is NOT a missing discriminator:

1. NO clean feature axis separates the 8 LOSER images from the 2
   WINNER images on the probed 28 features.

2. The W44-29 lift mechanism — the natural candidate based on the
   W44-91/96/166 discriminator pattern — produces marginal effects on
   3637739 and is already deployed on 4 of 5 measured LOSER images
   without closing the gap.

3. Two of the LOSER images (7062219, 1531677) already have multiple
   gates firing (W44-29 + variant Z) and STILL lose by +5-6% bytes —
   evidence that the entropy_mul mechanism is saturated.

The cluster's root cause is structural and falls into one of these
categories (all multi-day to multi-week to investigate):

- **CfL Newton parameter divergence** (already established Pareto-trade
  in W44-184). The W44-184 falsification chain showed that bit-exact
  libjxl Newton at default regresses 25/27 cells; the calibration is
  load-bearing. A 3637739-specific re-calibration would need to thread
  through the entire entropy_mul / AC strategy gate / buttloop seed /
  adaptive_quant lift chain.

- **AC strategy selection differences** not captured by the existing
  entropy_mul tables. Per W44-103/121/155, strategy selection on
  smooth photos diverges substantially from cjxl, even at matching
  per-region qac. Needs per-strategy AC dump + new mechanism class.

- **Butteraugli loop convergence at e8/e9**. Per W44-110/111/112,
  butteraugli RC differences are responsible for terminal SSIM2
  clusters. Same likely true for photo clusters at e8/e9.

- **Reconstruction pipeline divergence** (W44-178 → W44-184 falsified
  the obvious candidates for clic_097cb426; fresh hypothesis set
  needed). Cross-applies to 3637739 because both are smooth photos.

The W44-198 task gate (f) "no NEW Pareto-loser cells introduced" is
trivially satisfied by NOT shipping a fix. The task gate (e) "3637739
d=3-5 cells: bytes within ±2% AND SSIM2 ≥ -0.5" is NOT achievable
with the discriminator-based approach surveyed; bytes range +4-6% and
SSIM2 -1 to -3 across the cluster, and the surveyed lever moves at
most -1.7% bytes.

