## DO NOT (binding for future agents)

1. DO NOT re-attempt the W44-29 entropy_mul lift wrapping on 3637739
   with another mask/m3/edge_density gate combination. The forced-lift
   A/B is conclusive: the lift mechanism does not close the gap.

2. DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for the 3637739 cluster (per W44-66 user
   correction).

3. DO NOT raise W44_91_M3_COLOURFULNESS_MIN below 80 to admit 3637739
   (m3=12.21) — the existing measurements support 80 as the lower
   bound (per W44-91 follow-on notes), and 3637739 would slip through
   along with 1624487 (m3=66) which W44-91 protects.

4. DO NOT lower W44_166_VARIANT_Z_PHOTO_MASK_P25_MIN below 85.0 to
   admit 3637739 (mask_p25=55.83) — per W44-149 audit, the threshold
   has 11pp safety margin to nearest CONTROL.

5. DO NOT lower HIGH_D_PHOTO_SMOOTH_THRESHOLD above 50 to admit
   mask76_NOGATE class without re-running the forced-lift A/B AND
   getting closure on the LOSER_DOMINANT cells — the W44-29 mechanism
   is the lever for mask<50 cells, NOT mask>50.

## Follow-on candidates (NOT in scope for W44-198)

1. **Per-strategy AC dump for 3637739 e7 d=4** to test the AC
   strategy selection hypothesis. Reuse the W44-76 dump infrastructure.
   ETA: 1-2 days. EV: medium (would clarify whether the cluster is
   AC-strategy-driven vs cost-model-driven).

2. **3637739-specific entropy_mul re-calibration**. Per W44-184
   lesson, would need to thread through downstream calibration without
   destabilizing W44-29/91/96/166 wins. Multi-week.

3. **Root-cause butteraugli measurement divergence** (cross-crate,
   multi-week per W44-110/W44-111). Would obsolete this entire
   discriminator chain.

4. **CfL Newton per-image re-calibration**. Per W44-184, the default
   Newton is calibrated against entropy_mul tables; per-image
   re-calibration would require coupled optimization. Multi-week.

5. **Pareto-trade acceptance**. If the 3637739 cluster is structural,
   document it as a known pareto-trade in the cumulative bench. The
   bytes overhead is +5-6% in exchange for SSIM2 loss of -1 to -3 —
   not strictly worse, but a known weakness on the smooth-photo class.
